The file EVENTMAN.OPL is the example
Event Manager module. Also in this
directory you should find files Events1
to Events4 inclusive, which show (in
increasing complexity) how to use an
event manager like this.

There are just four routines in 
EventMan.OPL They are:

EMmake: -which initialises the event
         manager and calls your init
         code.
         
EMadd%: -which assigns your code a slot
         in the EM, and registers your
         function to be called back.
         
EMrem:  -which removes a slot previously
         assigned with EMadd%:
         
EMwait: -not normally called by your
         code. This is the main event
         loop, and you may call it for
         the purposes of background
         calculation.
         
         

Have fun!
Jezar.

